WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.830
Check every piece, sell honestly, and take photos that sell.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:08.440
This is the video for module three of Handmade Accessories for Sale.

3
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:16.200
Customers judge handmade work by the details: loose threads, glue marks, earrings that do not match.

4
00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:22.930
Your best piece is not your standard. Your standard is the worst piece you are willing to sell.

5
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:31.610
Trust is the real product. Most buyers come through people who know you, and one misleading description travels fast.

6
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:39.390
And online, the photo is the product. The buyer cannot touch your bag, so the picture must show it honestly.

7
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:51.730
Write a short finishing standard for each product, then check every piece against it. Step one. Inspect in good daylight or under a bright white bulb, never in dim light.

8
00:00:52.980 --> 00:01:01.410
Step two. Go through your standard line by line, and look at the back as well as the front. For example, ear wires closed with no gap.

9
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:09.800
Step three. Give a gentle stress test. Tug each strap, stretch each bracelet, give each ear wire a light pull.

10
00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:19.370
Step four. Sort it. Sell, fix, or seconds. Sell seconds clearly labelled at a lower price, never mixed with full-price stock.

11
00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:25.870
Step five. Write down every defect, even if you fix it. Your notes show the pattern.

12
00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:36.290
For example, Halima in Kano sold 30 stretch bracelets in a month. Four customers said theirs snapped or came undone within two weeks.

13
00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.740
She checked her notes. Three of the four broke at the knot.

14
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:49.180
She was using thin 0.5 mm cord for heavy glass beads, and trimming the ends before the glue was dry.

15
00:01:50.430 --> 00:02:00.480
So she changed her recipe card: 0.8 mm cord for beads 8 mm and above, pre-stretch every length, and trim only after the glue has dried.

16
00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:09.540
She replaced the four bracelets free and thanked each customer. Next month she sold 35 and heard of only one problem.

17
00:02:10.790 --> 00:02:19.920
Name materials exactly. For example, Ngozi changed her listing to say gold-tone ear wires, glass beads, and handmade in Aba.

18
00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:30.660
She removed gold, crystal and hypoallergenic, because her supplier could not confirm them. Never claim a metal or stone you cannot confirm.

19
00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:37.370
And never put a famous brand's logo on your work. That makes it a counterfeit, even if you made it by hand.

20
00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:53.660
Nickel is a common cause of skin allergy from jewellery. Offer earrings on confirmed metals for sensitive ears. If a customer reports irritation, advise her to stop wearing it, and offer a replacement on different findings.

21
00:02:54.910 --> 00:03:04.420
Beaded jewellery and small parts can choke babies and young children. Do not sell for that age group, and say not suitable for young children where it applies.

22
00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:17.090
And confirm payment in your own app before sending goods, because screenshots and SMS alerts can be faked. Agree price, delivery and your replacement policy in writing first.

23
00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:29.130
You do not need a professional camera. Clean the lens with a soft cloth. Use daylight from a window, not direct sun. Use a plain background, the same for every product.

24
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:37.120
Hold a white card opposite the window to lift shadows. Keep the phone steady, and move closer instead of zooming.

25
00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.150
And use no filters that change colours. The buyer must receive what she saw.

26
00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:49.410
Take the same five shots every time. The front on a plain background, and a side or back view.

27
00:03:50.660 --> 00:03:52.280
A close-up of your finishing.

28
00:03:53.530 --> 00:04:01.040
One worn or held to show size: earrings on an ear, a tote on a shoulder. Buyers always ask how big it is.

29
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:12.380
And the matching set together. Then write your description in the same order each time: name, size, materials, features, care, and price with delivery.

30
00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:27.630
To remember. Your standard is the worst piece you will sell. Inspect, stress test, sort and record. Name materials honestly. Confirm payment in your own app. And photograph in daylight with no colour filters.

31
00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:38.070
Now write your finishing standards and inspect your last batch. Rewrite three product descriptions honestly. Then photograph and list three products.

32
00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.360
Continue with the lessons below.
